{"base_rate":0.6509433962264151,"brier":0.325887893081761,"bss":-0.4342641467554511,"bss_hi":-0.24306302891583326,"bss_lo":-0.6688348607720458,"chart":{"base":[906.1,103.5],"fp":[636.6,393.0],"note":{"base":"skill -0.43 — higher than 4% of cities","fp":"low end +42pp, high end -6pp","rel":"promised 2% → rained 38%; promised 82% → rained 87%"},"rel":"73.9,302.1 122.8,219.1 207,186.9 340.5,135.2 581.2,90.9"},"country":"DM","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.3255188679245283,"ess":350.53151023128,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Roseau</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Roseau rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (93%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>22%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 636 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.43, ranked 205 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(201&ndash;209) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>37</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>54%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Roseau</b> <span class=\"muted\">Dominica</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>201&ndash;209\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>636 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Roseau &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.